# The image is one Go binary, so the context is hub/ and nothing else.
#
# Written as "exclude everything, then add back" rather than as a list of
# exclusions: the hub is now the only thing that gets built here, and a new
# top-level directory should not silently start bloating the context or busting
# the layer cache.
*
!hub/

# Inside hub/, the build reads the module files and the Go source, and (in the
# console stage) hub/web's own source and npm lockfile - not a prebuilt dist/,
# which the console stage produces itself.
#
# node_modules is ~200MB that never needs to cross the build context (npm ci
# installs it inside the stage instead); the Playwright suite needs a running
# hub and a browser, so it could not run in here anyway.
hub/web/node_modules/
hub/web/dist/
hub/web/e2e/
hub/web/test-results/
hub/web/playwright-report/
hub/web/*.tsbuildinfo

# Go tests do not run in the image build - CI runs them, with -race, which needs
# a toolchain this stage deliberately does not have.
hub/**/*_test.go
hub/**/testdata/

# Local state that must never reach a layer.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
